    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1200">

                <pb facs="1248" n="1236" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg1236"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">767.68119/8–945: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Turkey</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-09T12:00:00-04:00">August 9,
                            1945—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>813. Following is the text of the provisions concerning the “Black Sea Straits”
                    contained in the Protocol signed at Berlin on August 2, 1945:<anchor n="41"
                        xml:id="d1200-f1"/>
                </p>
                <pb facs="1249" n="1237" xml:id="pg1237"/>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“The Three Governments recognized that the Convention on the Straits
                        concluded at Montreux should be revised as failing to meet present-day
                        conditions.</p>
                    <p>It was agreed that as the next step the matter should be the subject of
                        direct conversations between each of the Three Governments and the Turkish
                        Government.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1200-f1" n="41" xml:id="d1200-f1-content">
                <p>This was article xvi of the Protocol of the Proceedings of the Berlin Conference:
                    see <ref target="frus1945Berlinv02#pg_1490">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Conference of Berlin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Potsdam</hi>) vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p. 1490</ref>,
                    and footnote 90.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
